  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...A dry cold front will move south across the region \ntonight bringing near normal temperatures and dry/occasionally \nbreezy conditions through early next week. Rain chances should \nincrease mid next week but forecast confidence remains low.\n\nA dry cold front will move south through the area tonight \nbringing temperatures back down to near normal into early next \nweek. Northeast winds are expected to be breezy at times, \nespecially near the coast. Unfortunately, rain chances appear to\nremain quite low, with the greatest chances near the coast \nstarting Sun night as a coastal trough develops and some upper \nenergy moves through. Hopefully rain chances increase mid next \nweek as advertised, although confidence still remains low given \nthat a rather amplified upper-level weather pattern is likely to\nevolve which typically creates more uncertainty.",
